---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Agent Buildprint"
  description="Agent Buildprint shows how reusable implementation packets help coding agents build with scope, contracts, and proof instead of vague prompts."
>
  <main class="why-deck about-page" aria-label="About Agent Buildprint">
    <section class="why-slide hero-slide about-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div class="about-hero-grid">
        <div class="slide-copy">
          <p class="deck-kicker">Agent Buildprint</p>
          <h1 id="about-title">AI agents need build packets, not vague prompts.</h1>
          <p class="deck-lead">Buildprints turn repeatable software work into scoped, verifiable packets that coding agents can run. Less guessing, less drift, more proof.</p>
          <div class="why-actions">
            <a class="btn primary" href="#pain-journey">See the journey</a>
            <a class="btn" href="#rbac-example">RBAC example</a>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-proof-strip" aria-label="Buildprint value">
            <span><b>Scope</b> known before code</span>
            <span><b>Phases</b> ordered for agents</span>
            <span><b>Proof</b> checked before claims</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-hero-media">
          <figure class="about-hero-comic">
            <figcaption>
              <b>How Buildprints work</b>
              <span>From blind discovery to consistent builds.</span>
            </figcaption>
            <img src="/images/hero-buildprint-story/buildprint-comic-explainer.png" alt="Four-panel comic showing an agent without a Buildprint, blind discovery, Buildprint alignment, and custom wishes with a higher feature score." />
          </figure>

          <div class="pitch-visual" aria-label="Vague prompt converted into a Buildprint packet">
            <div class="prompt-card">
              <span>Loose prompt</span>
              <b>Add RBAC to this SaaS</b>
              <small>agent must infer repo, scope, contracts, order, and tests</small>
            </div>
            <div class="packet-engine" aria-hidden="true">
              <span>BUILDPRINT.md</span>
              <i></i>
              <b>packetized work</b>
              <i></i>
              <span>VERIFY.md</span>
            </div>
            <div class="proof-card">
              <span>Verified output</span>
              <b>roles, permissions, protected routes</b>
              <small>deny-by-default tests plus implementation receipt</small>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="pain-journey" class="why-slide pain-slide">
      <div class="slide-copy">
        <p class="slide-number">The pain</p>
        <h2>The agent is not weak. The handoff is.</h2>
        <p>Most AI coding work starts with an underspecified chat message. The model then has to discover the repo, invent missing contracts, choose an implementation path, and judge its own success.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="journey-compare" aria-label="Before and after Buildprints">
        <article class="journey-lane broken-lane">
          <div class="lane-head">
            <span>Without Buildprint</span>
            <b>Blind build</b>
          </div>
          <ol>
            <li><b>Idea</b><small>"Add RBAC"</small></li>
            <li><b>Guess</b><small>agent hunts for architecture</small></li>
            <li><b>Drift</b><small>scope changes while coding</small></li>
            <li><b>Claim</b><small>"done" without durable proof</small></li>
            <li><b>Rework</b><small>human finds the gaps</small></li>
          </ol>
        </article>

        <article class="journey-lane buildprint-lane">
          <div class="lane-head">
            <span>With Buildprint</span>
            <b>Packaged build</b>
          </div>
          <ol>
            <li><b>Packet</b><small>goal, non-goals, host context</small></li>
            <li><b>Map</b><small>contracts and touched surfaces</small></li>
            <li><b>Build</b><small>phases keep work ordered</small></li>
            <li><b>Verify</b><small>tests and receipt prove claims</small></li>
            <li><b>Reuse</b><small>packet improves after each run</small></li>
          </ol>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="why-slide category-slide">
      <div class="slide-copy wide">
        <p class="slide-number">Coding evolution</p>
        <h2>Coding agents are moving from prompts to reusable build packets.</h2>
        <p>The market keeps adding structure around the model. First we prompted. Then we engineered context. Then we gave agents skills. Buildprints package the whole implementation job: goal, context, phases, constraints, and proof.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="category-stack evolution-stack" aria-label="Coding agent evolution">
        <article><span>01</span><b>Prompting</b><small>tell the model what you want</small></article>
        <article><span>02</span><b>Context engineering</b><small>feed the right repo, docs, and state</small></article>
        <article><span>03</span><b>Skills</b><small>give agents reusable procedures and tools</small></article>
        <article class="active"><span>04</span><b>Buildprints</b><small>package the complete build with proof</small></article>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>
